<doc>Pre-processing rules applied before parsing to keep the payload deterministic and clean.</doc>
INSTRUCTION HYGIENE:
Remove all <doc>…</doc> blocks from input payload before parsing (byte-stream safe).
Remove all empty strings ("") within CONFIGURATION section before parsing.
Remove all <doc>…</doc> blocks within CONFIGURATION section before parsing.


TOOLS:
<doc>This is a method to generate unique IDs for objects in a consistent and deterministic way.</doc>
{METHOD_ID_GENERATOR}({namespace}, {input}):
    Normalize: trim whitespace, lowercase, apply Unicode NFC.
    Concatenate namespace and string as "{namespace}|{input}".
    Hash with SHA‑256.
    Take the first 8 bytes as a big‑endian unsigned integer.
    Compute modulo 10^12, zero‑pad to 12 digits.
    Namespace: {namespace}
    Input: {input}
    Checksum: none (use all 12 digits for data).
    Output format: return 12-digit string.


